        {
          "name": "windowStartedAt",
          "ty_idx": 9
        },
        {
          "name": "lastBatchId",
          "ty_idx": 11
        }
      ],
      "description": "maxBatch / tonPerPayout / batchOverhead are settable because the real numbers\ncan only come from measuring gas on a live network.\n\nThe daily cap is a tumbling 24h window, not a true sliding one: a sliding\nwindow needs a ring buffer of timestamps and its cost grows per batch. The\ntradeoff is that up to 2x dailyCap can leave across a window boundary."
    },
